	(text "INPUT PROTECTION (record section 3). Self-acting: nothing depends on firmware or a\n  rail it protects. LTC4364-1 datasheet Figure 1 topology.\nF1 Nano2 453 15 A soldered: dead-short backstop. D801 SMBJ45CA (bidirectional:\n  survives a reversed supply) clamps the hot-plug ring.\nQ1 hot-swap FET on HGATE, Q2 ideal-diode FET on DGATE, common SOURCE: reverse\n  polarity AND reverse current blocked, so the regen clamp may sit at 44.5 V.\nR1 2 mOhm CSS2H, pseudo-Kelvin (SENSE and OUT on the inner-edge sense pads): 50 mV =\n  25 A limit (25 mV = 12.5 A folded back into a short). C802 22n C0G: ~0.23 ms in a\n  dead short (36 V x 12.5 A = 450 W in Q1), ~2.4 ms on a mild overload.\nC801 22n on HGATE: ~40 ms power-up ramp, ~0.4 A inrush into ~480 uF (4 x 82 uF bulk\n  + the drive's 150 uF + ceramics): the current limit and timer never engage at\n  start.\nR805/R806 402k/10k: output clamp 51.5 V, ABOVE the 44.5 V regen clamp so regen is\n  never read as an input surge (LTC4364-1 would latch).\nR802/R803/R804 374k/15k/10k: UV 20 V, OV 50 V. D802/D803 15 V gate zeners\n  (datasheet: required at >= 24 V). SHDN and ENOUT unused.\nLATCH-OFF (-1): a fault kills every rail; D6 + R30 27k from VIN_RAW light on FLT\n  with the board dark (FLT sinks <= 2 mA: 1.3 mA at 36 V). Power-cycle to clear.\nQ1/Q2 IPB042N10N3G: SOA ~55 A at 36 V for 0.2 ms (25 C); worst case (OUT just above\n  2.5 V, ~27 A at ~33 V, ~0.25 ms) keeps ~1.75x cold, ~1.35x hot. R2 = INA228 shunt,\n  WSK1216 true 4-terminal Kelvin."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 474.98 196.85 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8c2f64fc-b39e-4d7d-ab14-a4fe0fa67454")
	)
	(text "NOTES"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 472.44 190.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(thickness 0.508)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9e913635-d64d-4246-a2ad-7f6c8f1a1ab8")
	)
	(text "REGEN SHUNT (record section 5). Self-acting clamp, no firmware: U3 compares the\n  divided\n  bus to U4's 1.24 V; R503 hysteresis.\nR501/R502/R503 348k/10k/3.01M: ON 44.5 V, OFF 43.2 V (1.4 V hysteresis, the OSSM alt\n  board's value). Legal above the GST360A36's 37.8 V worst OVP only because the\n    input\n  section blocks reverse current.\nR509 || R510 || R511: Vishay D2TO35M 24R each = 8R (multi-pulse rated; element\n  isolated\n  from the tab, tabs to GND over 0.8 mm via fields into the back sink). ~7 W\n    continuous\n  total = 2.3 W each; 141 W peak = 47 W each.\nJ3 + JP501: external resistor. JP501 bridged = parallel with the on-board pair; cut\n  =\n  external replaces it. Size Q501 for the lowest combined R.\nD503 SS310 freewheels the resistor-loop current back to +BUS at turn-off, so trace\n  and\n  flying-lead inductance clamps at bus + 0.85 V. D501 stays as the backstop.\nU3 drives Q501's gate directly through R505 (TLV1805 push-pull, ~100 mA: ~0.7 us\n  edges,\n  ~0.25 W worst case in Q501; slow edges keep L di/dt small, no driver or snubber\n    needed).\n  R507/R508: gate pull-down + CLAMP_MON (2.98 V) to a P4 capture pin: on-time x V^2\n    / 8R =\n  clamp power, published over Valence. D502 lights while the clamp conducts. TH501\n    NTC\n  sits beside the D2TO35Ms -> SHUNT_TEMP (ADC1).\nU3 SHDN (active high) tied low: always armed. +12V from the 12 V buck, which starts\n  from\n  the bus by itself. C501 filters buck noise off the divider.\nQ501 IPB042N10N3G: its tab is the switch node (drain), NOT ground: give it its own\n  copper, not the grounded resistor via field."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 588.01 339.09 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a86e3424-4f67-43ed-a946-f6d1e351faf1")
	)
	(text "DRIVE IO (record sections 11-12; SPEC: 3.3 V RS485 non-isolated, quadrature via\n  74AHCT125, JST\n  GH signals).\nConnectors are the operator's: every off-board net ends in a named label (DRV_*, and\n  +5V_SYS\n  for the drive's 485_5V on comms pin 10; PU-/DIR-/COM are GND).\nU9 THVD1450 on a P4 UART in RS485 half-duplex mode, DE and /RE tied. R23 termination\n  fitted-\n  not-populated. D601 SM712 (-7/+12 V RS485 ESD) at the cable end.\nU10 on +5V_SYS (stamp pad 39, live on USB alone): TTL-threshold inputs take 3.3 V\n  GPIO, 5 V out\n  to the opto inputs. Gate 3 shifts LED_DATA to LED_DIN for the WS2812B (R601 pull-\n    down: low\n  while the P4 boots); gate 4 disabled.\nStatus: WR alarm and RDY are opto NPN to COM (= GND); ZO has no pin on the comms GH\n  and is not\n  wired: 10k pull-up to +3V3_SYS, 1k series into the P4 pin."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 474.98 394.97 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bb896c6d-1bee-4765-90df-773ce4e52ce7")
	)
	(text "RAILS (record section 10: independent bucks from +BUS). TPS54560B x3, one layout\n  three times; values from the datasheet's own design procedure (SLVSF00 section\n  8.2).\nDesign inputs: VIN 20-48 V (48 = supply OVP ceiling, covers the ~45 V clamp; part\n  rated 60 V), 4 A per rail, 400 kHz, half-load step held within 4 %.\n  fsw 400 kHz: RT 243k. Worst on-time 3.3 V at 48 V = 205 ns vs 135 ns minimum.\n    UVLO: 887k / 53.6k = start 20 V, stop 17 V.\n  12 V: L 18u, Cout 4x 22u/25V (~40u derated), FB 140k/10k = 12.00 V, comp 21.5k +\n    5.6n (fco ~35 kHz)\n   5 V: L 10u, Cout 3x 47u/10V (~85u derated), FB 52.3k/10k = 4.98 V, comp 15.8k +\n     6.8n (fco ~28 kHz)\n  3.3V: L 6.8u, Cout 3x 47u/10V (~113u derated), FB 31.6k/10k = 3.33 V, comp 13.7k +\n    6.8n (fco ~28 kHz)\n  Inductors: Isat >= 7.5 A (the switch current limit, datasheet's conservative\n    rule), shielded. Catch diode B560C (60 V 5 A, datasheet's pick). C106/C206/C306\n    = optional HF pole, DNP.\nLOADS (operator ruling 2026-09-22): LOGIC runs from the stamp's own rails so a USB-\n  only bench session powers the pulse path:\n  +5V_SYS = stamp pad 39 (its OR of VIN and USB): 74AHCT125, drive 485_5V, status\n    LED.   +3V3_SYS = stamp pad 28: INA228, THVD1450, every pull-up.\n  +5V feeds the stamp's VIN (pad 14) and 5 V accessories. +12V: regen clamp supply,\n    fan, 12 V accessory. +3V3_ACC: 3.3 V accessory only.\nLAYOUT: amp-class switch nodes vs the INA228 resolving +-5 uV is the likeliest\n  respin (section 10). Small SW nodes, far from R2 and U11."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 474.98 328.93 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c8f8dd31-cf16-4004-9d50-115b809158c0")
	)
	(text "POWER MONITOR (INA228)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 71.12 161.29 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(thickness 0.508)
